{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brokendown-graceless-pelican","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered while implementing e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a (typed reconciler mutation\npayload contracts, ADR 0107). Two producers construct (inbound, create)\nMutation payloads with different shapes:\n\n- differ.py's inbound-create path emits a FLAT dict of Jira fields (no\n  wrapper key): {f: v for f, v in jira_fields.items() if f not in excluded}.\n- binding_walk.py's ADOPT path emits a nested shape:\n  {\"fields\": _fields, \"jira_fields\": _fields}.\n\napply_inbound.py's _apply_inbound_create leaf already explicitly tolerates\nBOTH shapes (fields = payload.get(\"fields\") or payload), which is how this\nhas stayed silently correct in production. ADR 0107's typed\nInboundCreatePayload contract picks the flat shape (differ.py's) as\ncanonical, per e9d5's own corpus/contract decision -- so binding_walk.py's\nnested shape would fail typed validation today.\n\nThis is a pre-existing inconsistency, NOT introduced by e9d5 -- e9d5 only\ndocuments it (see the corpus README and e9d5's ticket comment recording\napproved intentional deltas) and does not reconcile it, since producer\nrewiring is ADR 0107's deferred \"Cut\" step and out of e9d5's own scope (AC7).\n\nSuggested follow-up: migrate binding_walk.py's ADOPT path to emit the flat\nshape (matching differ.py and the ADR 0107 InboundCreatePayload contract),\nthen simplify apply_inbound.py's _apply_inbound_create leaf to drop its\ndual-shape tolerance, before any producer is rewired to construct\nInboundCreatePayload directly (that \"Cut\" step is a separate, later\nticket).\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- binding_walk.py's ADOPT path and differ.py's inbound-create path agree on\n  payload shape, verified by a test asserting both producers emit the same\n  normalized shape for an equivalent inbound create.\n- apply_inbound.py's _apply_inbound_create no longer needs to tolerate two\n  shapes (or, if kept for defense-in-depth, the tolerance is documented as\n  intentional rather than load-bearing for a live producer).","id":"192c-d606-b72e-470f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Reconcile dual inbound-create payload shapes (differ.py flat vs binding_walk.py nested)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788109285932598001,"uuid":"f02e4229-cdd1-4324-a7be-67259006b037"}